{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    std::string email;\n    std::cin >> email;\n    \n    // Replace first \"at\" (starting from index 1)\n    auto it_at = std::search(email.begin() + 1, email.end(), \"at\", \"at\" + 2);\n    if (it_at != email.end()) {\n        email.erase(it_at, it_at + 2);\n        email.insert(it_at, \"@\");\n    }\n    \n    // Replace all \"dot\" sequences (starting from index 1, but not at very end)\n    auto pos = email.begin() + 1;\n    while (pos < email.end() - 2) {\n        auto it = std::search(pos, email.end() - 2, \"dot\", \"dot\" + 3);\n        if (it == email.end() - 2 && email.size() - (it - email.begin()) <= 3) break;\n        \n        if (it != email.end() && std::distance(it, email.end()) > 3) {\n            email.erase(it, it + 3);\n            email.insert(it, \".\");\n            pos = it + 1;\n        } else {\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    std::cout << email;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String email = scanner.next();\n        \n        // Replace first \"at\" (starting from index 1)\n        int atIndex = email.indexOf(\"at\", 1);\n        if (atIndex != -1) {\n            email = email.substring(0, atIndex) + \"@\" + email.substring(atIndex + 2);\n        }\n        \n        // Replace all \"dot\" sequences (starting from index 1, but not at very end)\n        int pos = 1;\n        while (pos < email.length() - 2) {\n            int dotIndex = email.indexOf(\"dot\", pos);\n            if (dotIndex == -1 || dotIndex > email.length() - 3) {\n                break;\n            }\n            \n            // Check if we're at the end (last 3 characters)\n            if (dotIndex >= email.length() - 3) {\n                break;\n            }\n            \n            email = email.substring(0, dotIndex) + \".\" + email.substring(dotIndex + 3);\n            pos = dotIndex + 1;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(email);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001805857609724626, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.674201020156033e-05, -2.288792165927589e-05, -0.0019300420535728335, -0.36052411794662476, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.564294092939235e-05, -1.9550132492440753e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -6.079655122448457e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00012814177898690104, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, -5.817244164063595e-05, -0.007195510435849428, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -1.6212332411669195e-